  "src": "pairs of same-colored foreground marker pixels s",
  "path": "straight horizontal or vertical interval between the two pixels in s",
  "trajectory": "paint every cell on the inclusive interval with s.color",
  "multi_step": "paint horizontal intervals before vertical intervals so vertical segment colors occupy crossings"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-30 rows x 10-20 cols, background 0
  segments:
    count: 5, each a distinct non-zero color (exactly 2 pixels per color in input)
    mix: 2-3 horizontal + 2-3 vertical [observed]
    orientation: two same-color pixels share a row (H) or column (V)
    length: 4-18 cells (inclusive endpoint-to-endpoint)
    uniqueness: no two H segments share a row; no two V segments share a column
    no-overlap: H segments must not overlap other H on shared row; V must not overlap other V on shared column
  crossings:
    count: 2-3 per example [observed]; at least 1 required
    rule: at H-V intersection, vertical color wins (V drawn after H)
  output: fill each inclusive interval between marker pair with its color; V overwrites H at crossings

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size in range. Choose 5 distinct non-zero colors.
    2. Decide orientation per color (2-3 H, 2-3 V).
    3. Assign each H segment a unique row; assign each V segment a unique column.
    4. For each H segment, pick column span (length 4-18) within grid bounds.
    5. For each V segment, pick row span (length 4-18) within grid bounds.
    6. Verify at least 1 H-V crossing exists; if not, adjust spans to create one.
    7. Verify no H-H overlap on any row and no V-V overlap on any column.
    8. Build output by drawing H segments first, then V segments (V wins at crossings).
    9. Derive input by keeping only the two endpoint pixels of each segment.
```
